CCDC Data License
Version 1.0, June 2026

Claude Code Data Collective (CCDC)

This license governs use of the curated corpus of sanitized Claude Code
session data made available by the Claude Code Data Collective (the
"Corpus"). By accessing, using, or distributing any part of the Corpus, You
agree to the terms below. If You do not agree, You may not use the Corpus.


PREAMBLE (non-binding)

This preamble explains intent and is not part of the operative terms; the
numbered sections below control. CCDC aims to make sanitized session data
broadly reusable, including commercially, while (a) requiring credit to the
Corpus, and (b) keeping downstream use aligned with Anthropic's Commercial
Terms by not permitting the Data to be used to train AI models that compete
with Anthropic. The Corpus contains material generated through Anthropic's
Claude products; recipients remain independently subject to Anthropic's own
terms governing that material. This license is assembled from clauses modeled
on widely used data and model licenses; it is offered as is and is not legal
advice.


1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Corpus" or "Data" means the session data and associated files made
available under this license, in whole or in part, with or without
modification.

1.2 "Contributor" means a person who submits Data to the Corpus.

1.3 "Licensor" means the CCDC maintainers, acting on behalf of Contributors,
who make the Corpus available under this license.

1.4 "You" means an individual or entity exercising rights under this license.

1.5 "Results" means any outcome of computational analysis of the Data —
including statistics, parsers, schemas, evaluations, and reports — but
excluding any AI Model as defined below.

1.6 "AI Model" means any machine-learning model, including its weights and
parameters, that generates text, code, or other content, and any system
built on such a model.

1.7 "Competing Model" means an AI Model that is intended to substitute for,
or compete with, the AI products or services offered by Anthropic, PBC.

1.8 "Share" means to provide the Data to a third party, by any means, with or
without modification.


2. GRANT OF RIGHTS

2.1 Subject to the conditions in Section 3, Licensor grants You a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive license to use, reproduce, modify, analyze, and
Share the Data, including for commercial purposes.

2.2 No Restrictions on Results. Except as stated in Section 3.2, this license
imposes no restriction on Your use, modification, or sharing of Results.
Analysis, parsing, research, and the development of tools that read or
describe the Data are expressly permitted. For the avoidance of doubt, an AI
Model is not a Result (see Sections 1.5 and 3.2).


3. CONDITIONS

3.1 Attribution. In any distribution of the Data, and in documentation
accompanying any product or service that incorporates the Data or material
Results derived from it, You must retain a copy of this license and include
the following notice: "Includes data from the Claude Code Data Collective
(CCDC), used under the CCDC Data License," together with a link to the Corpus
where practicable. You must not remove or alter attribution or provenance
notices accompanying the Data.

3.2 No Competing Models. You will not use the Data, or any output or material
derived from the Data, to train, fine-tune, develop, or improve a Competing
Model. For clarity, this Section does not restrict the creation of Results
(Section 2.2).

3.3 Pass-Through. Each time You Share the Data, You must (a) include a copy of
this license with it, (b) retain all attribution and provenance notices, and
(c) not offer or impose any term that removes or conflicts with the
conditions of this license. Each recipient of the Data from You receives the
rights and conditions in this license directly from Licensor. You may offer
additional or different terms for material You add, provided those terms do
not restrict the Data itself below the terms of this license.


